310
00:24:08,092 --> 00:24:13,392
母がなんかスーパーで買ってきてくれたポケモンパンを食べたよ。
I ate the Pokémon bread my mom bought at the supermarket.

311
00:24:13,892 --> 00:24:16,792
あの、チョコ蒸しパンみたいな、
That, like, chocolate steamed bread...

312
00:24:16,792 --> 00:24:18,692
蒸しパンみたいなやつ。
kind of like a steamed cake.

313
00:24:19,292 --> 00:24:20,992
ゼリーは冷やすの忘れてた。
I forgot to chill the jelly.

314
00:24:21,492 --> 00:24:24,692
ゼリーはね、今日冷やすの忘れすぎて食べてない。
I totally forgot to chill the jelly today, so I didn't eat it.

315
00:24:25,092 --> 00:24:29,192
冷蔵庫に何かないかなと思ったら母が買ってきてくれたポケモンパンがあったのじゃ。
I checked the fridge to see if there was anything, and found the Pokémon bread mom bought, noja.

316
00:24:29,492 --> 00:24:30,892
今日は何のシールだった？
"What sticker did you get today?"

317
00:24:30,892 --> 00:24:32,992
え、開ける？今！まだ開けてないの。
Eh, should I open it? Now! I haven't opened it yet.

318
00:24:33,592 --> 00:24:34,392
Okay.

319
00:24:34,592 --> 00:24:35,792
Let me see!

320
00:24:36,092 --> 00:24:37,692
開けてみるね。
I'll open it up.

321
00:24:38,292 --> 00:24:39,192
Wait.

322
00:24:39,792 --> 00:24:43,792
ジャジャジャジャーン！
Ta-da-da-daaa!

323
00:24:43,892 --> 00:24:45,592
ラウドボーン！
Skeledirge!

324
00:24:45,592 --> 00:24:47,592
ホゲータの最終進化か！
Fuecoco's final evolution!

325
00:24:47,692 --> 00:24:50,092
ラウドボーンだったのじゃ！
It was Skeledirge, noja!

326
00:24:50,692 --> 00:24:52,992
午後2時？あ、午後2時なんだ！
2:00 PM? Oh, it's 2:00 PM there!

327
00:24:54,192 --> 00:24:55,892
ラウドボーン！
Skeledirge!

328
00:24:56,692 --> 00:25:00,392
Mela-chi, your English was so good during the PEAK collab...

329
00:25:00,167 --> 00:25:01,567
the other day, you're amazing

330
00:25:01,567 --> 00:25:05,067
やったー！Thank youなのじゃー！やったのじゃー！
Yay! Thank you noja~! Yay noja~!

331
00:25:05,667 --> 00:25:07,967
ラウドボーン、そうそうそうそう。
Skeledirge, right, right, right, right.

332
00:25:07,967 --> 00:25:09,667
そう、まあ確かに強い。
Yeah, well, it's definitely strong.

333
00:25:09,767 --> 00:25:13,667
移動しながら聴いてる？やったー、Thank you！
Listening on the go? Yay, thank you!

334
00:25:13,667 --> 00:25:14,467
うん。
Yeah.

335
00:25:14,467 --> 00:25:15,667
御三家？
Starter Pokémon?

336
00:25:16,067 --> 00:25:20,667
炎属性？そう、炎タイプなの！一緒なのじゃー！
Fire attribute? Yes, Fire type! Just like me noja~!

337
00:25:20,967 --> 00:25:23,367
確かに、サラマンダーっぽいかもね。
True, it kind of looks like a salamander.

338
00:25:23,967 --> 00:25:26,667
よし、始めるかー！
Alright, let's get started!

339
00:25:26,667 --> 00:25:31,067
スタート English リスニング... え、「ルーシーと恐竜」じゃって！
Start English listening... Huh, it's "Lucy and the Dinosaurs" noja!

340
00:25:31,067 --> 00:25:33,567
お主ら、「ルーシーと恐竜」！
Hey everyone, "Lucy and the Dinosaurs"!

341
00:25:33,567 --> 00:25:38,367
ARKやってたから、あれなんじゃない？なんか、馴染みあるんじゃない？
Since you guys played ARK, aren't you familiar with this kind of thing?

342
00:25:38,567 --> 00:25:41,167
ダイナソー、ダイナソー。
Dinosaur, dinosaur.

343
00:25:41,467 --> 00:25:43,767
行くよ、お主ら。
Here we go, everyone.

344
00:25:43,767 --> 00:25:47,967
レッツスタート English stream なのじゃー！
Let's start the English stream noja~!

345
00:25:47,967 --> 00:25:48,967
よいしょ。
Here we go.

346
00:25:48,967 --> 00:25:50,967
Lucy and the Dinosaurs.

347
00:25:50,967 --> 00:25:54,167
Lucy and the Dinosaurs.

348
00:25:54,167 --> 00:25:57,967
音量はいいかな？こんなもんで一旦始めるのじゃ？
Is the volume alright? Shall we start like this for now noja?

349
00:25:57,967 --> 00:25:59,167
うん。
Yeah.

350
00:25:59,967 --> 00:26:02,167
ふん、ふん、ふん、ふん。
Mm, mm, mm, mm.

351
00:26:02,967 --> 00:26:04,067
よいしょ。
Here we go.

352
00:26:04,067 --> 00:26:06,567
Lucy opens her apartment door.

353
00:26:06,567 --> 00:26:13,367
Lucy opens her apartment door. ルーシーはアパートのドアを開けました。
"Lucy opens her apartment door." Lucy opened her apartment door.

354
00:26:13,367 --> 00:26:15,167
Hello, Junior.

355
00:26:15,167 --> 00:26:17,467
ハロー、ジュニア。
"Hello, Junior."

356
00:26:18,167 --> 00:26:21,967
わっぱ？よっ、わっぱ！よっ、わっぱ！
Kiddo? Yo, kiddo! Yo, kiddo!

357
00:26:21,967 --> 00:26:26,667
Hello! Can you help me write a report for school?

358
00:26:26,667 --> 00:26:32,567
ハロー！学校の宿題、手伝ってくれない？
"Hello! Can you help me with my school report?"

359
00:26:33,167 --> 00:26:35,167
Oh, yes.

360
00:26:35,167 --> 00:26:40,167
いいわよー。ルーシーおばあさん、yes. いいわよー。
"Of course~." Granny Lucy, yes. "Of course~."

361
00:26:40,167 --> 00:26:44,967
I'm a great writer. I have a very popular blog.

362
00:26:44,967 --> 00:26:46,967
ブリティッシュEnglishじゃん。
That's British English!

363
00:26:46,967 --> 00:26:48,167
なん... もう一回聴くか。
What... Let's listen again.

364
00:26:48,167 --> 00:26:52,667
I'm a great writer. I have a very popular blog.

365
00:26:52,667 --> 00:27:00,667
ブログ、あっ、私は超有名なブログを書くすごいライターなのよ。
Blog... Ah, "I'm a great writer who writes a super popular blog."

366
00:27:00,667 --> 00:27:08,667
ブログ書くの得意？えー、じゃあ、わしも戦えるかも。わしもかつてブログを書いていた時期があるから。
Good at writing blogs? Eh, then I might stand a chance too. Since I also had a period where I wrote blogs back then.

367
00:27:08,667 --> 00:27:14,467
わしもかつて はてなブログとかをやっていた時期があるから、ちょっと気持ちわかるかも。
Since I used to run a Hatena Blog back in the day, I might understand how she feels.

368
00:27:15,067 --> 00:27:19,967
え、なんか... ブリティッシュじゃない？ブリティッシュっぽくない？発音。
Wait, isn't that... British? Doesn't the pronunciation sound British?

369
00:27:20,667 --> 00:27:22,667
Do you read my blog?

370
00:27:22,667 --> 00:27:28,167
Do you read my blog? 子供になんでも読ませてんだ。
"Do you read my blog?" Why is she making a kid read whatever she writes?

371
00:27:28,167 --> 00:27:35,167
子供になんでも読ませてんだ。私のブログを読みたいかしら〜ん？
Why is she making a kid read whatever she writes? "Would you like to read my blog~?"

372
00:27:35,667 --> 00:27:41,967
子供に、いかが、読んでいいブログか？子供が読んでいいブログなのか？
Is that really a blog suitable for a child to read? Is it okay for kids to read?

373
00:27:42,467 --> 00:27:46,967
「Do you read」... あ、読んでますかの方？読んでますかの方なのかな？
"Do you read"... Oh, does it mean "Do you read it?" Maybe it means "Do you read it?"

374
00:27:46,967 --> 00:27:54,967
読みたいかしら、じゃない？「Do you read」だから、読む？読むか？読むー？か。
Not "Would you like to read?" It's "Do you read", so "Do you read it?" "Will you read it?" Or "Do you reeead it?"

375
00:27:55,167 --> 00:27:56,167
No.

376
00:27:56,167 --> 00:27:57,167
No.

377
00:27:57,167 --> 00:28:04,667
読んでませんか？読んだことある？読んだ？読んでない。読むかい？読まない。
"Don't you read it?" "Have you read it before?" "Did you read it?" "Haven't read it." "Wanna read it?" "Nope."

378
00:28:04,667 --> 00:28:07,167
I have a lot of books.

379
00:28:07,167 --> 00:28:09,667
たくさんの本を持っているわ。
"I have a lot of books."

380
00:28:10,667 --> 00:28:13,667
Do you need my books for research?

381
00:28:13,667 --> 00:28:20,167
Do you need my books for... あ、ブログ作戦失敗したから、本いっぱいあるよ。
"Do you need my books for..." Ah, since her blog plan failed, "I have lots of books!"

382
00:28:20,167 --> 00:28:28,167
本いっぱいあるけど、あの、宿題用に使うー？
"I have lots of books, so um, do you need them for homework?"

383
00:28:29,967 --> 00:28:32,667
I don't need your books.

384
00:28:32,667 --> 00:28:38,167
なんか振られまくりじゃない、ルーシー？ルーシー、断られまくりじゃない？
Isn't Lucy getting rejected left and right? Isn't Lucy getting repeatedly shot down?

385
00:28:38,167 --> 00:28:42,967
I don't need your books. 別にいらんのじゃー。
"I don't need your books." I don't need them at all noja~.

386
00:28:42,967 --> 00:28:45,467
What is your report about?

387
00:28:45,467 --> 00:28:49,967
あなたは何についてのレポートを書いてるの？
"What is your report about?"

388
00:28:49,967 --> 00:28:55,167
めらさんも本持ってる？そんなにいっぱい持ってないね。あんま本読まないのじゃ。
Do I have books? Not that many. I don't really read books noja.

389
00:28:55,167 --> 00:28:56,667
Dinosaurs.

390
00:28:56,667 --> 00:29:01,467
恐竜！あ、非常に、非常に子供らしい。そうじゃよね。
Dinosaurs! Ah, very, very typical for a kid. Totally relatable, right?

391
00:29:01,467 --> 00:29:07,967
別に恐竜の本とか、あんまルーシー読まなそうだもんな。恐竜の本が読みたいのじゃ。
Lucy doesn't seem like the type to read dinosaur books anyway. He wants dinosaur books noja.

392
00:29:07,967 --> 00:29:10,667
Why do you want to talk to me?

393
00:29:10,667 --> 00:29:16,167
なんで... なんでわしに、じゃあ話しかけたん？
Why... Why did you talk to me then?

394
00:29:16,167 --> 00:29:18,667
Why do you want to talk to me?

395
00:29:18,667 --> 00:29:22,667
何について話してほしいか？Why do you want to talk to me?
What do you want to talk about? "Why do you want to talk to me?"

396
00:29:22,667 --> 00:29:25,667
「Why」、でも「なぜ」。「なぜ」だよ。
"Why", but it means "why". It means "why".

397
00:29:25,667 --> 00:29:29,667
Why do you want to talk to me?

398
00:29:29,667 --> 00:29:34,667
なんで私に喋って欲しかったのか？
Why did you want to talk to me?

399
00:29:36,167 --> 00:29:39,967
Why... Why do you want talk to me?
Why... "Why do you want to talk to me?"

400
00:29:39,967 --> 00:29:44,367
なんで私に話しかけたの？
"Why did you talk to me?"

401
00:29:44,367 --> 00:29:48,967
は？なんで恐竜なのに私に話しかけたの？なんで？
Huh? If it's about dinosaurs, why did you talk to me? Why?

402
00:29:49,167 --> 00:29:51,967
Because you are very old.

403
00:29:56,667 --> 00:30:01,967
そういうことか！「なんで、なんで恐竜について私に話しかけたんですか？」って言ったら...
So that's why! When she asked, "Why did you ask me about dinosaurs?"...

404
00:30:02,725 --> 00:30:06,275
Because you are very old.

405
00:30:07,175 --> 00:30:08,875
だって、だって...
I mean, because...

406
00:30:09,475 --> 00:30:12,225
おばあちゃんだから恐竜見たかなと思って...
I thought maybe she saw dinosaurs since she's a grandma...

407
00:30:12,225 --> 00:30:16,075
そこまで、そこまでじゃないよ！
Not THAT old!

408
00:30:16,075 --> 00:30:18,875
Rude だよ、Rude、失礼だよ。
That's rude! Rude, that's disrespectful.

409
00:30:19,275 --> 00:30:21,475
何だ？喧嘩売ってんのか？
What, are you picking a fight?

410
00:30:22,175 --> 00:30:25,875
いや〜お年寄りだから恐竜も詳しいかなと思って、
"No, I just thought since you're old, you might know a lot about dinosaurs..."

411
00:30:25,875 --> 00:30:30,075
おばあちゃんが子供の頃は恐竜いたんでしょ？
"Dinosaurs were around when you were a kid, right, Grandma?"

412
00:30:33,075 --> 00:30:36,875
めらが子供の時も恐竜いないけどな、別に。
Dinosaurs weren't around when Mela was a kid either, though.

413
00:30:38,075 --> 00:30:43,875
When I am young でも、I was young でも、no dinosaurs だけどな。
Whether "When I am young" or "I was young," there were no dinosaurs, though.

414
00:30:44,875 --> 00:30:46,275
わしもいない。
Not in my time either.

415
00:30:46,875 --> 00:30:50,275
めら、Can you tell me... tell us about the dinosaurs?
"Mela, can you tell me... tell us about dinosaurs?"

416
00:30:50,275 --> 00:30:55,375
No, I don't know! I never see dinosaurs.
No, I don't know! I've never seen dinosaurs.

417
00:30:55,875 --> 00:31:00,575
なんか恐竜の化石...化石？何だ、ひょ...なんか、骨、骨みたいなさ、
Like dinosaur fossils... Fossils? What is it... like bones, bone-like things,

418
00:31:00,575 --> 00:31:04,875
博物館みたいなのはさ、見たけど、それ以外は知らないのじゃ。
I've seen them in museums and stuff, but other than that, I don't know, noja.

419
00:31:07,475 --> 00:31:09,875
Salamanders dinosaurs? No.

420
00:31:09,875 --> 00:31:12,075
サラマンダーはダイナソーじゃないよ。
Salamanders aren't dinosaurs.

421
00:31:12,275 --> 00:31:14,775
Salamanders no dinosaurs.
Salamanders are no dinosaurs.

422
00:31:15,275 --> 00:31:17,575
だって恐竜はいたじゃろ？
After all, dinosaurs actually existed, right?

423
00:31:17,575 --> 00:31:20,575
サラマンダーの方が架空なのじゃ、どちらかと言うとね。
Salamanders are more of a mythical thing, comparatively speaking.

424
00:31:21,075 --> 00:31:23,075
恐竜は火吹けないじゃろ？
Dinosaurs can't breathe fire, right?

425
00:31:23,075 --> 00:31:26,075
サラマンダーは火吹けるのじゃ、から違う。
Salamanders can breathe fire, noja! So they're different.

426
00:31:28,075 --> 00:31:29,875
鳥類じゃないよ、わし。
I'm not an avian!

427
00:31:30,475 --> 00:31:32,875
Yes, dinosaurs birds.

428
00:31:33,375 --> 00:31:36,275
そう、恐竜は鳥じゃけど、わし鳥じゃないのじゃ。
Right, dinosaurs are birds, but I'm not a bird, noja.

429
00:31:36,275 --> 00:31:38,875
I'm not bird なのじゃ。
I'm not a bird, noja.

430
00:31:40,275 --> 00:31:42,875
You know a lot of dinosaurs, right?

431
00:31:42,975 --> 00:31:46,875
たくさんの恐竜知ってるでしょ、ねえ、おばあちゃん。
"You know a lot of dinosaurs, right, Grandma?"

432
00:31:47,375 --> 00:31:49,375
Goodbye, Junior.

433
00:31:49,375 --> 00:31:50,875
Goodbye, Junior.

434
00:31:50,875 --> 00:31:52,475
Goodbye, Junior.

435
00:31:52,875 --> 00:31:55,075
バイバイ、バイバイ。
Bye-bye. Bye-bye.

436
00:31:55,075 --> 00:31:58,075
もういい！「もういい」はありがとうございましたか？
"Enough!" Does "Enough" mean thank you?

437
00:31:58,075 --> 00:32:00,575
「もういい」はありがとうございましたか？
Does "I've had enough" mean thank you?

438
00:32:02,075 --> 00:32:04,875
なるほどね、なるほどね、かわいそうに。
I see, I see. Poor thing.

439
00:32:05,075 --> 00:32:09,075
たくさんの、a lot of。でしょ、right。
"Lots of" is "a lot of." "Right?" is "right."

440
00:32:10,075 --> 00:32:13,875
必要ありません、don't need。調べもの、research。
"Don't need" is "don't need." "Look up" is "research."

441
00:32:13,875 --> 00:32:16,375
開けます、opens。
"Open" is "opens."

442
00:32:16,575 --> 00:32:18,875
怒ってどっか行っちゃった。
She got mad and walked off.

443
00:32:18,875 --> 00:32:20,575
クソガキ相手に...
At a brat...

444
00:32:20,575 --> 00:32:24,075
クソガキ相手に怒って、「もういい！もういいのじゃ、さらばじゃ！」って言っちゃった。
She got mad at a little brat and went, "Enough! That's enough, farewell!"

445
00:32:24,575 --> 00:32:27,575
Are salamanders and dinosaurs friends, Mela?

446
00:32:27,575 --> 00:32:32,075
No, I never... I never see dinosaurs.
No, I never... I've never seen dinosaurs.

447
00:32:33,575 --> 00:32:36,875
right、rightをもっと使えるようになりたいのじゃ。
"Right"... I want to get better at using "right," noja.

448
00:32:38,475 --> 00:32:41,875
かわいそうにおばあちゃん。そんな古くないよね。
Poor grandma. She's not that old.

449
00:32:42,475 --> 00:32:46,275
大人気ない？まあ確かに大人気なくはある。大人気なくはあるが、
Immature? Well, true, that was pretty immature. It was immature, but...

450
00:32:46,275 --> 00:32:49,075
まあコンディションというものがね、人間はありますからね。
well, humans have good and bad days, you know.

451
00:32:49,075 --> 00:32:51,875
イライラしやすい日というのもありますからね。
There are days when you get easily annoyed.

452
00:32:52,575 --> 00:32:58,575
あの、普段は流せることが、イライラしやすい日じゃと流せないみたいなことも大にして起こり得るので、
You know, things you can usually shrug off might get to you on an irritable day; that happens all the time,

453
00:32:58,575 --> 00:33:01,275
そういう日だったのでしょう、彼女は。
so it was probably just one of those days for her.

454
00:33:02,275 --> 00:33:05,475
次！ネクスト！
Next! Next!

455
00:33:05,475 --> 00:33:09,075
わしは別にいいよ。わしはおばあちゃん扱いされてもいいよ。
I don't really mind. I don't mind being treated like a grandma.

456
00:33:09,075 --> 00:33:13,875
I'm... OK if you guys say me...
I'm... OK if you guys call me...

457
00:33:13,875 --> 00:33:18,875
grandma？でもいいよ。
...grandma? That's fine too.

458
00:33:18,875 --> 00:33:23,575
なぜならわしは本当におぬしらより長生きしてるからね。
Because I've genuinely lived longer than all of you, after all.

459
00:33:26,575 --> 00:33:29,575
いいよ、別にわしは。
It's fine, I really don't mind.

460
00:33:29,575 --> 00:33:33,075
わしグランマ...グランマのじゃ？
Me, grandma... Grandma-noja?

461
00:33:33,075 --> 00:33:35,875
お子様扱い？まあそれもいいよ。
Treated like a kid? Well, that's fine too.

462
00:33:35,875 --> 00:33:38,575
好きなようにするといいよ。
Treat me however you like.

463
00:33:41,075 --> 00:33:46,075
Yes！グランマのじゃ？Yes、グランマのじゃ。うん、Yes！
Yes! Grandma-noja? Yes, Grandma-noja. Yeah, yes!

464
00:33:47,075 --> 00:33:54,075
グランマでも、あの、キッズでもいいよ。何でもいいよ！
Grandma or, um, a kid is fine. Anything is fine!

465
00:33:55,075 --> 00:33:58,875
好きに...消費するといいのじゃ。
Feel free to... consume me however you like, noja.

466
00:33:59,275 --> 00:34:02,075
お姫様でもいいよ、プリンセスでもいいよ。
A princess is fine too. Calling me princess is fine too.

467
00:34:02,075 --> 00:34:05,575
Princess Mela is great, too.

468
00:34:07,075 --> 00:34:09,275
何でもいいよ。
Anything is fine.

469
00:34:11,875 --> 00:34:14,875
好きなように、のじゃ。
However you like, noja.

470
00:34:15,675 --> 00:34:17,575
次行くか。
Shall we move to the next one?

471
00:34:18,075 --> 00:34:20,575
えっとな、リスニングかな？
Umm, listening practice, maybe?

